/F2 13 Tf (4. Station protection) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(Ostbank P-7 and Quayside are the two stations at risk. At Stage 2 crews fit the) Tj T*
(demountable aluminium barriers at both sites. The barrier sections, posts and seals are) Tj T*
(stored in the Quayside depot, and the target time to install them at both stations is) Tj T*
(forty minutes from the crews arriving.) Tj T*
T*
(At Stage 3 the electrical supply to the Quayside motor control centre is isolated before) Tj T*
(water reaches the plinth, and the harbour district is fed from Hollow Lane through the) Tj T*
(cross-connection valve on Mill Street. Ostbank keeps running unless water enters the) Tj T*
(screening house, in which case the intake is closed and the settling lagoon is drawn) Tj T*
(down to keep Millrace in service.) Tj T*
T*
(Portable pumps are positioned inside each barrier line to remove seepage. Sandbags are a) Tj T*
(last resort and are used only to close gaps the barriers cannot reach.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf (5. Staffing) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(From Stage 2 each at-risk station is staffed continuously by two people. Staff must wear) Tj T*
(lifejackets within ten metres of the water and must never enter flowing flood water.) Tj T*
(Shifts are limited to twelve hours, with a relief crew called at least two hours before) Tj T*
(handover.) Tj T*
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
