/F2 13 Tf (6. Public notices) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(If flood water enters a treatment process or a service reservoir, or if pressure is lost) Tj T*
(in a district for more than four hours, a precautionary boil-water notice is issued for) Tj T*
(the affected area after consultation with the health inspectorate.) Tj T*
T*
(Notices are published on the board's website, sent by text message to registered) Tj T*
(customers, and delivered by hand to care homes and schools.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf (7. Recovery) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(Before a flooded station returns to service it is cleaned, inspected by an electrician) Tj T*
(and disinfected. Mains in the affected area are flushed and chlorinated. A boil-water) Tj T*
(notice may be lifted only after two consecutive sets of samples, taken at least 24 hours) Tj T*
(apart, are clear of indicator bacteria.) Tj T*
T*
/F2 13 Tf (8. Debrief) Tj T* /F1 11 Tf
T*
(A debrief is held within ten working days of the stand-down. Its findings, with named) Tj T*
(owners and dates, are added to the improvement log, and this procedure is reviewed) Tj T*
(against them.) Tj T*
T*
ET
endstream
endobj
